# Python has several built-in types: int (integers), float (decimals), str (text), bool (True/False), list (ordered collections), tuple (immutable lists), dict (key-value pairs), and set (unique values).
# Type hints can be added using annotations like `def greet(name: str) -> str:` to specify expected types for better code clarity and IDE support.
# Python is dynamically typed, meaning variables can change types at runtime: x = 5 (int), then x = "hello" (str) is valid, unlike statically typed languages.
